      "explanation": "When 0.5 g of non-volatile solute dissolve into 39 gm of benzene then relative lowering of vapour pressure occurs. Hence, vapour pressure decreases from 650 mmHg to 640 mmHg.<br><br>Given, vapour pressure of solvent (p<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 436.6 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) = 650 mmHg<br><br>Vapour pressure of solution (p<sub>s</sub>) = 640 mmHg<br><br>Weight of non-volatile solute = 0.5 g<br><br>Weight of solvent (benzene) = 39 g<br><br>From relative lowering of vapour pressure,<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.091ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"28.253ex\" height=\"3.253ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -955.9 12488 1438\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(220,477.2) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(536,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(939.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2